These vectors are vendored verbatim from

    https://github.com/sirosfoundation/siros-dc-matcher
    crates/siros-dc-matcher-core/tests/vectors/circuit_zk

commit d68cf52b77e62b0dd0b37311dcff37d1e8fd5362 (v0.8.0)

They are the shared conformance set for every implementation of the
circuit_zk query planner - the Rust matcher, the Kotlin and Swift SDKs, and
this verifier. Vendored rather than fetched so the test suite does not
depend on the network.

A vendored snapshot goes stale silently: if the matcher's request shape
moves, these tests keep passing against the old one. Refresh with

    make vendor-circuit-zk-vectors

and commit the result, which updates this file's commit line too.
